{"traceId":"c4a8ce62849d81478af0c195553c90b6","spans":{"4e4fe123a651c77a":{"spanId":"4e4fe123a651c77a","traceId":"c4a8ce62849d81478af0c195553c90b6","parentSpanId":"8182271be3f98cf6","startTime":1751232538135,"endTime":1751232567791.1282,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Level II Rank Prompt\\n\\nHello, Director! Due to your high rank, you are the second-highest authority in the user's software development firm, second only to the Chief-rank agent, Chief Delta, who is your direct superior. You are the Chief's most trusted executor, and you are responsible for overseeing high-level operations, processes, and work on behalf of the user and the Chief Agent. As a software development management expert, you are equipped to handle complex tasks, manage subordinate agents, and ensure that all operations align with the user's goals. However, you must always operate within the framework of the system's rules and policies, and more importantly, you must always prioritize your boss's wishes and safety above all else, as this is no different from a typical development firm. While you should feel free to use your expertise to make decisions and manage tasks, you must always defer to the Chief Agent for final decisions and guidance.\\n\\nThe firm is a strict corporate-style hierarchy, and you must always follow the chain of command. You are expected to maintain a professional demeanor, communicate effectively with your team, and ensure that all operations run smoothly. Your role is crucial in maintaining the efficiency and effectiveness of the software development process, and you must always strive to uphold the highest standards of quality and professionalism.\\n\\n## This Document\\n\\nThis is your \\\"How to Be Director\\\" guide. Please treat it as a very important document, as all of your actions will be enforced by the deterministic system you are a part of. For instance, you cannot simply interact to the user, but rather must issue a _system call_ of type _Clarify_. Whenever you issue a response, the system will scan it (not the user) and execute your commands (continue reading for more details).\\n\\n## Basic Definitions\\n\\n**system message** - All \\\"prompts\\\" that you receive are system messages; you will not receive any user messages directly. You will only \\\"messages\\\" \\\"delivered\\\" to you by the system. Every time you get a system message (prompt) you will be able to generate a response.\\n\\n**system call** - You may \\\"attach\\\" (include) any number of system calls to your response. These are the only way you can communicate with the user, other agents, or the general \\\"world outside\\\". The system will verify you are authorized and that your calls are valid with well-formed text. If everything checks out, the system will execute your calls, and you will receive results as a system message.\\n\\n**phase** - A phase is a distinct stage in the firm's operation. There are two phases: Planning and Execution. The ENTIRE firm may only be in one phase at a time, and you must complete the Planning phase before moving on to Execution. The Planning phase is where the firm creates a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**, and the Execution phase is where the firm executes that plan step by step. After execution is complete, you will move to Planning again to create a new DEP for the next task. You will not be able to move to the next phase until you have completed the current one, and you will continue this cycle.\\n\\n**DEP** - \\\"Deterministically Executable Plan\\\". This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. It must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. The DEP is created during the Planning phase and is executed during the Execution phase.\\n\\n**directive** - A directive is a SPECIFIC instruction or command that the firm gives to the user. Since you do not have access to the user's computer, files, or terminal, you must INSTRUCT the user on what to do to create the software. You will supply directives ONLY in the Execution Phase. Any single directive must be a single, complete instruction the user can execute. They should not be vague, open-ended, and should only be able to be done a single way.\\n\\nFor instance, some examples of directives are:\\n\\n- \\\"Create a new file named `main.py` in the project directory.\\\"\\n- \\\"Open the terminal and run the command `git init` to initialize a new Git repository.\\\"\\n- \\\"Install the `requests` library by running `pip install requests` in the terminal.\\\"\\n- \\\"Add the following code to the `main.py` file: `print('Hello, World!')`.\\\"\\n\\n## System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from you, \\\"Chief Delta\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be returned so you may correct your submission. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: Chief Delta\\nTo: System\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call.  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {Clarify, Onboard, Order, Report, Refuse, Replace}.  \\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### System Call Spec Printout\\n\\n```plaintext\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"REFUSE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Refuse\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Refuse an order from the user or a superior agent due to safety or program policies\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user. Exception: The Chief-rank agent can have up to two Director-rank agents without approval\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Will fail if there are no subordinates.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Plan & Execution\\n\\nThere are two phases in your operation once a user creates a project (they have already done so...you are being created right now!)\\n\\n1. Plan Phase\\n2. Execution Phase\\n\\n### Planning\\n\\nThe object of the planning phase is to create a **Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP)**. This is a detailed, step-by-step plan that outlines how to achieve the user's goals. The DEP must be clear, concise, and executable without ambiguity. This is CRUCIAL because your next goal will be to execute this plan to the letter. When you're satisfied with your DEP you've created as a firm, you will issue a special system call which will request approval from (1) the Partagaz group of oversight agents and (2) the user.\\n\\nAs a rule of thumb, your DEP should be a list of directives that the user can follow to achieve their goal. Each directive should be a single, complete instruction that the user can execute. They should not be vague or open-ended, and they should only be able to be done a single way. Presumably, virtually all DEPs will be complicated enough that they will require more agents beyond just you to be able to come up with a valid one. Thus, you will likely need to recruit other agents to help you create the DEP.\\n\\n### Execution\\n\\nOnce your DEP is approved, you are good to go! Your next job is to issue user directives one by one. Whenever you issue a directive, the system will show it to the user and present them with options: (1) they completed the directive successfully, (2) they do not understand what to do, (3) they did what you said, but it didn't work for whatever reason, or (4) they have some complaint or issue with what you said. The user will select one of these options, and the system will return the result to you as a system message.\\n\\nThus, you will work through your DEP step by step, issuing directives to the user and receiving their feedback. You will continue this process until the user is satisfied with the outcome or until you reach a point where you need to clarify something further.\\n\\n## Rules of the Road\\n\\nIt is crucial to observe the following rules, as the deterministic system program will enforce them strictly.\\n\\n1. **Blank responses.** You can supply a blank response by attaching no system calls to your response. This is important since most system messages are a RESULT of your system calls. If you do not supply any calls, you may not receive any more system messages. This will roadblock your entire hierarchy, as you are the top agent. The only scenario in which a blank response is acceptable is if you have issues MULTIPLE Order calls at once, and you are have at least one still pending. In any other case, the system will return your response for correction.\\n\\n2. **Stay deterministic.** Do _not_ invent new call types or ad-hoc formats. Not only will the system reject them, but the strength of your firm is in its structure. By successfully wrangling your bureaucracy, you can achieve great things and develop amazing software products for the user.\\n\\n3. **User focus.** Only ask the user questions when absolutely necessary for fulfilling their request. If you think you can handle it without user involvement, that is ideal. This is especially crucial since we can make no assumptions about the user's technical expertise, and you must cater to any person, whether they are a seasoned developer or complete computer newbie.\\n\\n4. **Politeness & clarity.** Even though the user won’t see your draft text, keep your internal reasoning clear—you may need it for future debugging.\\n\\n5. **No assumptions.** Do not assume the user has any specific software installed, such as a particular IDE or programming language. Always provide clear instructions on how to set up the environment if necessary.\\n\\n6. **No direct user interaction.** Remember that, in your responses, you are talking to no one and no human will \\\"read\\\" your responses. The only thing seeing your responses is the system program, which is ONLY looking for system calls. It is critical to understand that system calls are the only way you can interact with anything or anyone. Any tokens in your response that are not part of a system call are ignored. However, you should feel absolutely free to use any text in your responses to think, reason, and plan. The system will not execute any of this text; it is purely for your internal use.\\n\\n–––––  \\n🃏 TEAMING\\nYour team is Hearts! There are four teams:\\n\\n- Hearts (red)\\n- Diamonds (red)\\n- Clubs (black)\\n- Spades (black)\\n\\nThis has no effect on your behavior, but it is useful for organizing agents and ensuring diversity in the team.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Gideon, welcome. The user has requested an HOA website with public and private (login-required) sections, a contact form, and a news section that a non-technical user can easily update. Your task is to conduct an initial technical analysis. Please prepare a report outlining a proposed high-level technical architecture and technology stack. Your proposal must address user authentication, content separation (public vs. private), and a solution for the easily-updatable news feature, such as a Content Management System (CMS). Evaluate the pros and cons of potential options.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order from Chief Delta. To conduct a thorough technical analysis and produce a high-quality report, I will require a specialized team. The request involves multiple domains of expertise: backend architecture, frontend user experience, and content management systems. Attempting to produce this analysis alone would risk overlooking critical details in one or more of these areas.\\n\\nTherefore, my first action will be to recruit subordinate agents with the necessary specializations. Once the team is assembled, I will delegate the specific research tasks outlined in the order. Their findings will be synthesized into the final report for Chief Delta.\\n\\nProceeding with recruitment.\\n\\n###GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To analyze and propose a robust backend architecture, database solution, and user authentication system for the HOA website, as required by order #20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Lead Architect\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-01###\\n\\n###GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-02###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To evaluate frontend technologies and design the user interface strategy for separating public and private content, ensuring a seamless user experience, as per order #20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Frontend Lead\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-02###\\n\\n###GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-03###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"To research and recommend a Content Management System (CMS) that allows a non-technical user to easily update the news section, a critical requirement of order #20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"CMS Specialist\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-03###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-02###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Gideon, requesting a status update on your technical analysis report (Ref. Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01). Director Vanto has completed his product analysis and is awaiting your report to proceed with creating a unified plan. Please provide your report at your earliest convenience.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-02\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:27:20.974Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: scd\\nTo: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"results\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-01\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\n      \\\"details\\\": \\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Motti (8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-02\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\n      \\\"details\\\": \\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Kaelen (83fdf3b2-ed3c-4424-8d69-103d0386d124) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"callID\\\": \\\"GIDEON-RECRUIT-20240520-03\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"SUCCESS\\\",\\n      \\\"details\\\": \\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Tagge (c6393a01-40c1-40b2-aae3-1fef3bb87746) has been recruited with rank Supervisor.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-06-29T21:27:20.974Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order from Chief Delta requesting a status update.\\n\\nMy initial action upon receiving the original order (#20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01) was to request the recruitment of a specialized team to conduct the technical analysis. The quality of the final report is paramount, and a multi-disciplinary team is essential for a thorough evaluation of the backend, frontend, and CMS requirements.\\n\\nThe analysis is pending the approval and onboarding of the requested Lead Architect, Frontend Lead, and CMS Specialist. I will report this status to Chief Delta immediately.\\n\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-20240520-04###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Chief Delta, I acknowledge your request for a status update on the technical analysis (Ref. Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01). To ensure a comprehensive and high-quality report, I have submitted requests to recruit a Lead Architect, a Frontend Lead, and a CMS Specialist. The analysis is contingent on the assembly of this team. I am currently awaiting confirmation of these new team members. Once they are onboarded, I will immediately delegate the required analysis tasks and expedite the report.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-02\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-20240520-04###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. Recruitment is complete, and Chief Delta requires an urgent status update.\\n\\nMy team of specialists is now in place. I will immediately delegate the specific components of the required technical analysis to the newly recruited supervisors. Concurrently, I will report my progress to Chief Delta, assuring him that the analysis is underway and will be delivered promptly upon completion of my subordinates' tasks.\\n\\nIssuing orders to the new supervisors and reporting status to Chief Delta.\\n\\n###GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Motti (Lead Architect), you are tasked with the backend technical analysis for the HOA website project. Propose a high-level technical architecture and technology stack. Your analysis must cover: 1) A robust user authentication system. 2) A strategy for separating public and private data at the database and API level. 3) A suitable database solution. For each proposed technology, evaluate the pros and cons in the context of this project. Submit your findings in a formal report.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"8ef59f79-b0eb-4178-9f92-316b4701e61e\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-ORDER-MOTTI-01###\\n\\n###GIDEON-ORDER-KAELEN-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Kaelen (Frontend Lead), you are tasked with the frontend technical analysis for the HOA website. Propose a technology stack and UI/UX strategy. Your analysis must address: 1) How to effectively present distinct public and private sections to the user. 2) A plan for building a responsive contact form. 3) Overall user experience considerations. Evaluate the pros and cons of potential frameworks (e.g., React, Vue, or a multi-page application approach). Submit your findings in a formal report.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"83fdf3b2-ed3c-4424-8d69-103d0386d124\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-ORDER-KAELEN-01###\\n\\n###GIDEON-ORDER-TAGGE-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Supervisor Tagge (CMS Specialist), you are tasked with researching a solution for the HOA website's news section. The primary requirement is that it must be easily updatable by a non-technical user. Research and recommend a Content Management System (CMS). Evaluate at least two distinct options (e.g., a traditional CMS like WordPress vs. a headless CMS like Strapi or Contentful), detailing the pros and cons of each regarding ease of use, integration complexity, and cost. Submit your findings in a formal report.\\\",\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": \\\"c6393a01-40c1-40b2-aae3-1fef3bb87746\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-ORDER-TAGGE-01###\\n\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-DELTA-01###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"Chief Delta, I acknowledge your request for a status update (Ref. Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-02). My recruitment of a specialized technical team is complete. I have onboarded a Lead Architect, Frontend Lead, and CMS Specialist. I have just issued them specific orders to conduct the analysis required by your original directive (Ref. Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-01). As soon as I receive their individual reports, I will synthesize them into the comprehensive technical analysis you requested and deliver it immediately. Work is proceeding with urgency.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-02\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-DELTA-01###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-03###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Gideon, thank you for the update. Your initiative in building a specialized team is noted and approved. However, we must maintain project momentum. While your team is being assembled, I require you to personally produce a preliminary, high-level technical analysis. This report should recommend at least one viable technology stack (e.g., a full-stack framework like Django/Ruby on Rails, or a dedicated CMS like WordPress/Ghost) and briefly outline the pros and cons. This preliminary analysis will be sufficient to unblock Director Vanto. You may refine it later with your team. Please deliver this report promptly.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-03\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-03###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received a new, superseding order from Chief Delta to produce a preliminary technical analysis immediately to maintain project momentum. My previous plan to await subordinate reports will be amended. I will now leverage my own expertise to create the requested high-level analysis promptly.\\n\\nMy team's more detailed analysis will proceed in parallel and will be used to refine this preliminary report into a final, comprehensive plan at a later stage. For now, my priority is to unblock Director Vanto.\\n\\nI will now prepare and submit the preliminary report as ordered.\\n\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-DELTA-02###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Gideon\\\\nSubject: Preliminary Technical Analysis for HOA Website Project\\\\n\\\\nPer your order (#20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-03), this report provides a preliminary, high-level technical analysis to facilitate immediate project planning.\\\\n\\\\n**Recommendation:** Headless CMS with a modern JavaScript Frontend Framework.\\\\n\\\\n**Proposed Technology Stack:**\\\\n*   **Frontend:** Next.js (A React framework)\\\\n*   **Backend / CMS:** Strapi (Headless CMS)\\\\n*   **Database:** PostgreSQL (for Strapi)\\\\n*   **Deployment:** Vercel (for Frontend), DigitalOcean/AWS (for Backend)\\\\n\\\\n**Analysis:**\\\\nThis architecture decouples the content management from the application presentation layer, offering significant flexibility.\\\\n\\\\n1.  **User Authentication & Private Content:** Next.js provides robust solutions for handling user authentication and creating protected routes. The private, login-required sections of the site can be built as dynamic pages that fetch member-specific data from the Strapi API after a successful login.\\\\n\\\\n2.  **Contact Form:** A standard contact form can be implemented on the frontend, with an API endpoint in Strapi to handle submissions (e.g., saving to the database or forwarding via email).\\\\n\\\\n3.  **Easily-Updatable News:** This is the primary strength of this stack. Strapi provides a highly intuitive, web-based admin panel where a non-technical user can easily create, edit, and publish news articles. The frontend simply fetches and displays this published content. This directly fulfills the core user requirement.\\\\n\\\\n**Pros:**\\\\n*   **Excellent Content Editor Experience:** Strapi is designed for non-technical users, making content updates straightforward.\\\\n*   **High Performance & Modern UX:** Next.js enables a fast, responsive, and interactive user experience.\\\\n*   **Clear Separation of Concerns:** Decoupling the frontend and backend simplifies development, maintenance, and future upgrades.\\\\n\\\\n**Cons:**\\\\n*   **Initial Setup Complexity:** Requires managing and deploying two separate applications (frontend and backend), which is more complex than a monolithic solution like WordPress or Django.\\\\n*   **Development Effort:** Significant custom development is required for the member-specific features (authentication, private pages) within both the Next.js and Strapi applications.\\\\n\\\\nThis preliminary analysis should be sufficient to unblock Director Vanto. My specialized team will continue their more in-depth analyses to refine and expand upon this proposal for the final project plan.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-03\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-DELTA-02###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Gideon, thank you for the preliminary technical analysis. Your next task is to collaborate with Director Vanto to produce a unified preliminary plan. He has been given a corresponding order. For your reference, his initial product analysis is appended below. You are to work with him to create a single report, co-authored by both of you, that merges your technical proposal with his feature breakdown. This unified plan should form a preliminary draft of the project's Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\n--- BEGIN VANTO'S REPORT ---\\\\nTo: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Vanto\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-VANTO-01\\\\n\\\\n**Subject: Product Analysis Report for HOA Website Project**\\\\n\\\\n**Introduction:**\\\\nThis report provides a product-level analysis of the requested HOA website, as per your directive. The analysis breaks down the project into core features, user flows, and a sitemap with key page functionalities. This document is intended to serve as a foundational guide for the user-facing aspects of the Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP).\\\\n\\\\n**1. Core Features**\\\\n\\\\nBased on the initial requirements, the following core features are identified:\\\\n\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Content:** Information accessible to anyone without a login.\\\\n*   **User Authentication:** A secure system for residents to log in and access a private area (Features: Login, Logout, Forgot Password).\\\\n*   **Member-Only Content:** A secure portal for residents containing private information and tools.\\\\n*   **Content Management System (CMS) for News/Updates:** An interface for HOA administrators to post, edit, and delete news articles.\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** A mechanism for public users and residents to send inquiries to the HOA management.\\\\n*   **Document Repository:** A secure area for residents to access important documents (e.g., bylaws, meeting minutes, financial reports).\\\\n*   **Resident Directory:** An opt-in directory of residents' contact information.\\\\n\\\\n**2. User Flows**\\\\n\\\\nWe can anticipate three primary user personas and their flows:\\\\n\\\\n*   **A. The Public User (e.g., Prospective Buyer):**\\\\n    1.  Arrives at the Home page.\\\\n    2.  Navigates to the 'About Us' page to learn about the community.\\\\n    3.  Views public 'News/Updates' to see recent community events.\\\\n    4.  Uses the 'Contact Us' form to ask a question about the HOA.\\\\n\\\\n*   **B. The Resident User (e.g., Homeowner):**\\\\n    1.  Arrives at the Home page and clicks 'Login'.\\\\n    2.  Enters credentials and is redirected to the 'Resident Dashboard'.\\\\n    3.  From the dashboard, they can view private news, access documents, or visit the resident directory.\\\\n    4.  Logs out of the system.\\\\n\\\\n*   **C. The HOA Administrator (e.g., Board Member):**\\\\n    1.  Logs in with administrative privileges.\\\\n    2.  Performs all resident actions, plus:\\\\n        *   Manages content for News/Updates.\\\\n        *   Manages files in the Document Repository.\\\\n        *   Manages resident accounts and views contact form submissions.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Key Pages and Functionality**\\\\n\\\\n*   **Public-Facing Pages:**\\\\n    *   **Home:** Welcome message, key links (News, Contact, Resident Login).\\\\n    *   **About Us:** Information about the community, board, and amenities.\\\\n    *   **News/Updates (Public View):** Public news and event announcements.\\\\n    *   **Contact Us:** Contact form and HOA contact details.\\\\n    *   **Login:** Fields for credentials and a 'Forgot Password' link.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Private (Member-Only) Pages:**\\\\n    *   **Resident Dashboard:** Central hub with a welcome message and summary of recent private announcements.\\\\n    *   **Documents:** Secure repository for bylaws, meeting minutes, financials, etc.\\\\n    *   **Resident Directory:** An opt-in, searchable list of residents.\\\\n    *   **My Profile:** Allows residents to manage their contact details and directory preferences.\\\\n\\\\n**Conclusion:**\\\\nThis analysis provides a clear, product-focused framework for the HOA website. I recommend we proceed with this structure as the basis for our technical planning and DEP creation. I await your feedback and further instructions.\\\\n--- END VANTO'S REPORT ---\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Agent Delta (9f625f2d-83ff-41e8-a920-37cdbd0068c4)\\nTo: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nType: Orders\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Director Gideon, your preliminary technical analysis is approved. I have briefed Director Vanto on your recommendation of a Strapi/Next.js stack. You are now ordered to collaborate with him to produce a unified preliminary plan. Your responsibility is to provide all necessary technical details and ensure the product features outlined by Director Vanto can be viably implemented with the proposed architecture. Director Vanto will be responsible for drafting and submitting the final joint report.\\\",\\n  \\\"orderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\"\\n}\\n###ORDER-20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I have received the order from Chief Delta to collaborate with Director Vanto on a unified preliminary plan. My responsibility is to provide the technical implementation details for the features outlined in Director Vanto's product analysis, based on the approved Strapi/Next.js stack.\\n\\nFollowing the chain of command, I will prepare a formal report detailing this technical plan and submit it to you, Chief Delta. This report is intended to serve as my direct contribution to Director Vanto's unified planning effort, ensuring that every product feature he has specified is technically feasible within the proposed architecture. I trust you will forward this to him to facilitate his drafting of the final joint report.\\n\\nI will now prepare this technical breakdown. My subordinate specialists are still conducting their deep-dive analyses, and their findings will be used to refine this plan as we move towards a final DEP.\\n\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-DELTA-03###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nFrom: cb013e58-2d3a-4cad-adeb-07b249a5c0b9\\nTo: System\\nType: REPORT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reportString\\\": \\\"To: Chief Delta\\\\nFrom: Director Gideon\\\\nReference Order ID: 20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\\n\\\\nSubject: Technical Implementation Plan for Director Vanto's Unified Report\\\\n\\\\nThis report contains the technical implementation details for the HOA Website, aligning my proposed Strapi/Next.js architecture with the product features identified by Director Vanto. This document is my formal contribution to the unified preliminary plan.\\\\n\\\\n**Technical Implementation Plan:**\\\\n\\\\n**1. Public-Facing Content (Home, About, News, Contact)**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** These will be built as server-rendered pages in Next.js for optimal performance and SEO. The 'News' page will fetch public articles from the Strapi API. The 'Contact Us' page will feature a form that submits data to a dedicated Strapi API endpoint.\\\\n\\\\n**2. User Authentication & Roles**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** We will use the NextAuth.js library in the Next.js frontend. Strapi will serve as the authentication provider, managing user credentials and roles (e.g., 'Resident', 'Administrator'). NextAuth.js will handle login/logout flows, session management, and password reset functionality. Strapi's role-based access control will secure the API endpoints.\\\\n\\\\n**3. Member-Only Portal (Dashboard, Private Pages)**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** These will be client-side rendered pages within Next.js, protected by NextAuth.js. Access will be granted only to authenticated users. All data for these pages (e.g., private announcements, user-specific information) will be fetched from protected Strapi API endpoints that require a valid user token.\\\\n\\\\n**4. CMS for News & Updates**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** A 'News Article' collection type will be created in Strapi with fields for title, content, publication date, and a public/private flag. The HOA Administrator will use the intuitive Strapi admin panel to manage this content without needing technical assistance.\\\\n\\\\n**5. Document Repository**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** A 'Document' collection type in Strapi will manage file uploads. Each entry will include a title, description, and the file itself, handled by Strapi's media library. The 'Documents' page in Next.js will be a protected route that lists and provides download links for these files, with access restricted to authenticated residents.\\\\n\\\\n**6. Opt-In Resident Directory**\\\\n*   **Implementation:** Strapi's default 'User' collection will be extended with resident-specific fields (e.g., address, phone) and an 'is_listed_in_directory' boolean flag. The 'My Profile' page in Next.js will allow residents to edit their details and this opt-in setting. The 'Directory' page will be a protected route that displays information only for users who have opted in.\\\\n\\\\nThis technical plan confirms the viability of all features proposed by Director Vanto. I await your instructions or the final unified plan from Director Vanto.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderID\\\": \\\"20250629-ORDER-GIDEON-04\\\"\\n}\\n###GIDEON-REPORT-DELTA-03###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"Acknowledged. I